# T3 fix: Partial MPTC membership check at TypeVar binding time.
#
# Storing $+ as a variable bypasses check_arithmetic (which handles direct [+ x y] calls)
# and routes through the general check_call_with_scheme path instead. When "hello" is
# unified with the Addable-constrained TypeVar _tN, check_constraints_on_var fires the
# T3 membership check: Str is not arithmetic, so a constraint-violation warning is emitted
# at TypeVar BINDING TIME rather than waiting for FD improvement.
#
# The body is wrapped in a zero-arg function so the call is type-checked but not evaluated,
# avoiding a runtime error from [+ "hello" 1].
[add-fn: $+
 bad-call: [fn [] [add-fn "hello" 1]]]
=== out
Dict({"add-fn": Builtin(+), "bad-call": Function()})
=== warn
type Str does not satisfy arithmetic constraint Addable — expected Number, Int, or Float
